dition that for some  can be debilitating heather jane is  trying to maintain hope i'm a very  different person now and i've been  forever changed by this experience two  years after her first infection the  toronto woman is now recovering from  covid yet again  unsure of how this second round will  impact her long-term health heather urex  west global news calgary  coming up it's one of the most pristine  marine ecosystems on earth why the  weddell sea off antarctica is under  threat and worth saving  [Music]  a state of emergency has been declared  in an area of thailand after an oil  slick washed up on a stretch of beach  near ray yong about two hours south of  bangkok it's estimated between to 50  tons of oil leaked tuesday night in the  gulf of thailand from an underwater hose  used to load tankers the leak was  stopped within hours but oil hit local  beaches today there are fears this will  decimate the local tourism industry  already struggling to recover from the  pandemic  scientists are calling for protection  for a barely understood part of the  world a piece of antarctica called the  weddle sea it sits at the top of the  continent southeast of argentina  scientists say making it a marine  protected area would shield it not just  from climate change but from human  threats and as ross lord reports experts  say there's not much time left  at a time when climate change is making  waters in the antarctic warmer and  rearranging ocean currents the wittle  sea has been mostly immune it's an area  that's going to have hopefully a more or  less intact ecosystem for much longer  than we're going to have in other parts  of the antarctic more time for penguins  and other species to adapt to whatever  changes they eventually encounter  but researchers and conservationists say  marine animals need protection from  other threats like large-scale fishing  they're pushing for the weddell sea to  be declared a marine protected area  governments have failed for several  years to create an ocean sanctuary in  the world of sea this cannot be another  year of delay  and continued harm to penguin  populations and other wildlife here in  the antarctic  marine protected areas are becoming  widespread by some estimates almost  eight percent of the ocean is under some  sort of protection including 14  locations in canada at 2.8 million  square kilometers the weddell sea would  be the largest marine protected area on  earth but holdouts including china and  russia are reluctant to give up their  fishing interests as the political  wrangling continues so does research  like determining how penguin populations  are holding up in the current  environment we need to do science on the  ground first that's why we're in a place  like this a penguin colony to understand  change and what's here already so that  we can protect the species where they  need it most bolstering their argument  for conservation fully aware that what  ultimately happens in the weddell sea is  out of their hands  ross lord global news  next finding refuge in play time afghan  refugees get out of quarantine and have  some fun exploring their new home  [Music]  that is ash barty celebrating big after  serving up success on home soil ending a  44 year long grand slam drought the 25  year old became the first aussie to win  the australian open since christine  o'neill captured the women's singles  title back in 1978  and she did it without losing a single  set  this is just a dream come true for me  and i'm i'm so proud to be in aussie so  thank you so much everyone  the women's world number one recovered  from being 5-1 down in the second set to  beat danielle collins 6-3 7-6 barty now  has three grand slam titles under her  belt  [Applause]  how about that indeed the greatest  quarterback to ever play the game is  apparently calling it a career the nfl  confirms 44 year old tom brady is  expected to retire after 22 seasons and  seven super bowls including last year's  victory 